{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 1428.3, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Continue fresh observation in a new domain per D083. Remaining untested package registries: Go pkg.go.dev, Pub.dev (Dart/Flutter), CocoaPods, CPAN, Docker Hub. Also consider VS Code Marketplace, Chrome Web Store, or other extension marketplaces with install metrics.", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": true, "summary": "Designed and executed fresh observation experiment E103 on Hex.pm (Elixir/Erlang package registry) per D083. Collected 200 packages (100 need-related via keyword searches, 100 random via default listing). All four gates PASS: G1 (sample=200≥100), G2 (Mann-Whitney U p≈0.000, Cliff's δ=0.861), G3 (Wilson LB=0.946, 99/100 need-related above random median), G4 (both categories represented). Need-related packages show dramatically higher 30-day downloads: median 80,078 vs 365 (220×), mean 644K vs 37K (17×). View-count principle generalizes strongly to Hex.pm, joining PyPI, NPM, and NuGet as package registries where the principle holds. Updated STATE.md and STATE-next-actions.md with findings.", "unlogged_changes": 7}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 17, "session": "2026-10-11-025-design-and-run-a-fresh-observation-exper", "ts": "2026-10-11T16:43:03+00:00"}
